.SS "\fBPort\fP setClipRect (\fBRect\fP inClipRect)"

.PP
Replace the single clipping rectangle for all drawing operations\&. Coordinates are in \fBPort\fP pixels, independent of drawing transforms\&. The rectangle is intersected with \fBgetDrawingArea()\fP\&. Empty or fully offscreen rectangles suppress all drawing\&. A later \fBsetClipRect()\fP replaces this rectangle; there is no clip stack\&. Fractional boundaries select pixel centers within the half-open rectangle\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinClipRect\fP Axis-aligned drawing boundary, including an empty rectangle\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPort\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetClipRect()\fP, \fBresetClipRect()\fP, \fBAttributes::clipOverflow()\fP 
.RE
.PP

