.SS "\fBPort\fP setDrawingOrigin (\fBPoint\fP origin)"

.PP
Set the \fBPort\fP coordinate at the top left of an offscreen surface\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIorigin\fP Finite coordinates for the drawing area's top left\&. Initially (0, 0)\&.
.RE
.PP
Pixel dimensions and stored pixels do not change\&. \fBgetDrawingArea()\fP reports the new origin and the clip resets to that area\&. \fBDrawing\fP and clipping now use those coordinates; \fBImage\fP pixel coordinates remain zero-based\&. This supports rendering a View into a reusable surface without changing its layout coordinates\&. Onscreen ports and nonfinite origins are rejected with an error\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires a \fBPort\fP from \fBGraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort()\fP\&. 

.PP
API stability: 2 — Evolving\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBclear()\fP, \fBgetDrawingArea()\fP, \fBImage::Image(Port, boolean)\fP 
.RE
.PP

